<title>BELGIUM: Belgian yr/yr inflation 1.26 pct in April.</title>
<headline>Belgian yr/yr inflation 1.26 pct in April.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian Economics Ministry released the following data on inflation -</p>
<p>    BELGIAN CONSUMER PRICES     April	March	April 1996</p>
<p>    Index (base 100=1988)	 123.91     123.94     122.37</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (in pct)	-0.02	-0.45	+0.17</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change (in pct)	  +1.26	+1.46	+2.04</p>
<p>NOTE - consensus forecast for April CPI +1.37 percent.</p>
<p>    Health index *		  121.33     121.31</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (in pct)	+0.02	-0.57</p>
<p>NOTE - * excludes unhealthy products such as tobacco, alcohol and petrol, is used for inflation adjustments of rents and wages.</p>
<p>The ministry said price rises were mainly seen for holiday villages, while for fresh fruit, petrol and fresh vegetables lower prices were recorded.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
